<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13811" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπο-στᾰσία</span></b> , ἡ, late
		form for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπόστασις,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>defection, revolt,</i>
			v.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				7.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>Vit.</u>
				10
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Galb.</u>
				1
			</span></i>; esp. in religious sense, <i>rebellion against God,
				apostasy,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Jo.</u>
				22.22
			</span></i>, <i>2 Ep.Th.</i><i><span class="en">
				2.3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>departure, disappearance,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Olymp.
				<u>in Mete.</u>
				320.2
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>distinguishing,</i> c. gen., <i><span class="en">
				Elias
				<u>in Cat.</u>
				119.7
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>distance, </i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Archim.
				<u>Aren.</u>
				1.5
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
</div>